From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 07:21:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 151/225] ASoC: sprd: fix i2s0 DMA request UID (ap_dma 4/3, not
 5/6)

The i2s0 stream set up its DMA and ran, but ap_dma never completed a
single transfer (GIC SPI24 IRQ count stayed 0) and writes failed with
-EIO after filling the buffer -- the DMA was armed on the wrong request
line so the i2s never triggered it.

sprd-dma takes the hardware request UID from the DT phandle cell
(sprd_dma_filter_fn -> schan->dev_id -> SPRD_DMA_GLB_REQ_UID). The vendor
DT cell was 5/6 but the vendor pcm driver overrode it via
dma_slave_config.slave_id = DMA_REQ_IIS0_TX(4)/DMA_REQ_IIS0_RX(3). That
slave_id field was removed from dma_slave_config upstream, so the ported
pcm driver can't override -- the cell itself must be the real UID.

Set dmas = <&ap_dma 4 &ap_dma 3> so the channel arms on the request line
the i2s0 TX/RX FIFOs actually assert.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/sprd-sound-fe-be.dtsi | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/sprd-sound-fe-be.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/sprd-sound-fe-be.dtsi
index fb679f7ca..eb190e61b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/sprd-sound-fe-be.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/sprd-sound-fe-be.dtsi
@@ -1130,7 +1130,16 @@ codec {
 	sprd_pcm_iis: sprd-pcm-iis {
 		compatible = "unisoc,sharkl5-pcm-platform";
 		#sound-dai-cells = <0>;
-		dmas = <&ap_dma 5 &ap_dma 6>;
+		/*
+		 * The sprd-dma cell is the hardware request UID (sprd_dma_filter_fn
+		 * -> schan->dev_id). The vendor DT used 5/6 but the vendor pcm
+		 * overrode it via the now-removed dma_slave_config.slave_id with
+		 * the real UIDs DMA_REQ_IIS0_TX=4 / DMA_REQ_IIS0_RX=3. Mainline has
+		 * no slave_id override, so the cell itself must carry 4/3 or the
+		 * channel arms on the wrong request line and the i2s never triggers
+		 * the DMA (ap_dma completes nothing -> underrun/-EIO).
+		 */
+		dmas = <&ap_dma 4 &ap_dma 3>;
 		dma-names = "iis0_tx", "iis0_rx";
 		sprd,dma-2stage-usecase = <2>;
 		sprd,node-count-2stage-level-1 = <1>;
